# Append-only change trunk streams (ADR-0014, ADR-0015, ADR-0038, ADR-0045).
# Only `skillset release apply` appends to them; change commands write
# write-once pending files under .skillset/changes/events/ instead, which the
# pattern below does not match and which merge as ordinary added files.
# Records are only ever added at the end, so restacking a release branch onto
# trunk should keep both sides' records instead of conflicting: union replays
# the branch's appended block after trunk's. `union` is a built-in git strategy:
# unlike a custom merge driver it needs no per-clone `git config` registration,
# so it also applies in CI, fresh clones, and worktrees, though GitHub's
# server-side merge does not honor it. `bun run change-stream:guard` checks what
# union cannot — valid JSONL, unique ids, write-once pending files, and that
# trunk's stream is an in-order prefix of the working copy.
.skillset/changes/*.jsonl merge=union

# Generated output and skillset.lock files carry no merge attribute (ADR-0045).
# Each lock line belongs to one unit, so a text merge of branches that changed
# different units is the merged render; where both branches changed the same
# unit, git conflicts and `skillset resolve` regenerates. `bun run
# generated-merge-policy:guard` checks that no generated path is marked
# `-merge` or `union`.
